atherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total and waits longer between each one.\n\n**Behaviour:**\n- Only HTTP 503 triggers a retry. Any other HTTP error, such as a 500, is raised straight away.\n- The wait between attempts is `backoff * 2**n`. With the new `backoff=0.5` default in `__init__`, that means 0.5s and then 1s. Existing callers don't need to change anything.\n- If all 3 attempts get a 503, that last `HTTPError` is raised to the caller.\n- The response from each failed 503 attempt is closed before the next try.\n- Timeouts and connection errors are not retried, since only 503 was asked for.\n\n**Checked against a real local HTTP server:**\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | returns the JSON | 3 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | raises `HTTPError 503` | 3 |\n| 500 | raises `HTTPError 500` | 1 |\n| 200 | returns the JSON | 1 |\n\nThe repo had no test suite, so this was a one-off script and no test file was added.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34796, "requests_cache_write": 179027, "requests_cost_usd": 0.9395502, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1870, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial28", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 114, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:52:39.935141+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 146.273, "t_checker_s": 2.43, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "est